WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:57.000
<i>Have the courage, set sail</i>
<i>and believe and we will see</i>

3
00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.180
<i>A glimpse of the sun</i>
<i>rising on our tomorrow.</i>

4
00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:06.170
But they were blocked
by the Priest Shura,

5
00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.640
As the four members
of Luffy's exploration team

6
00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.050
know precisely the location
of the gold this island

7
00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:15.060
has kept secret for 400 years,
they set their sights on it

8
00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:18.810
and head south from
the sacrificial altar.

9
00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.860
South. I mean.

10
00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:25.860
Straight, uh, directly
south, or down.

11
00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:29.490
Opposite of north.
Or, uh... Whatever.

12
00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:34.760
<b>Pirate Luffy vs. Berserker Wyper</b>

13
00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:34.770
but against a real guy? Hm.

14
00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.770
Sounds like the island is
having it's fair share of drama.

15
00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.490
I bet these homes were
built so far out from the city

16
00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:43.530
in the hopes of greater
longevity with crops.

17
00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:45.410
But it looks like all this
brush swallowed up

18
00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:46.070
the mortar and brick.

19
00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:47.280
I hope the city's still there.

20
00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.490
What are you doing here, woman?

21
00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:58.000
You should be aware
that this is the path

22
00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:02.580
to God's Shrine! Proceeding any
further would be insolent!

23
00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.340
Would you get down?

24
00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:07.720
Do you even have a clue as

25
00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.290
to the archaeological
significance of these ruins?

26
00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.630
They're priceless.

27
00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.050
How dare you talk back!

28
00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:15.510
What are you doing here anyway?

29
00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.390
You have some kind
of business with me?

30
00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.760
Hmph!
Yes, simple business, actually.

31
00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.380
I've been charged by God
to eliminate any Shandorians

32
00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.590
or Blue Sea people
I find with my Axe Dial!

33
00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:31.400
Heh. Seis Fleurs!

34
00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.610
And with a twist.

35
00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.930
Such a lack of respect.

36
00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.040
And you call yourself divine?

37
00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:02.420
These guys are gonna
be the end of us.

38
00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.420
So far, they've managed
to kill a lot more of us

39
00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:06.460
than we have of them.

40
00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:07.760
South should be to the right,

41
00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.760
so if I keep to the right,
I should find it.

42
00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.430
That's one of
those Blue Sea People

43
00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.020
Wyper was talking about.

44
00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.230
Better go take him out.

45
00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:20.730
A guerilla!

46
00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:22.230
And he looks pissed.

47
00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.430
Die!

48
00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.160
What's your problem?

49
00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:34.840
You fellas have some serious
anger management issues.

50
00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:41.180
P-Please, no! I surrender!

51
00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:46.060
I give up! I lose, you win.
Just, please, don't kill me!

52
00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:46.850
I-I want to...

53
00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:52.730
Not again.

54
00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:54.280
Listen, nutcase.

55
00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:57.340
If you're not a Priest, then go
find another goat to shoot!

56
00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:59.570
I'm in a hurry here!

57
00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:27.280
All right. What's the deal
with these glowing pistols?

58
00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:31.010
Where'd he go?

59
00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.350
Couldn't have gotten far.

60
00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:52.700
You put up a good fight.

61
00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:55.410
I'm almost sorry I
underestimated you.

62
00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:05.420
Well, thanks, pal.
But I should apologize to you.

63
00:07:05.510 --> 00:07:07.470
I took you for a loser.

64
00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:24.510
He never moved his feet!

65
00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:32.130
Pagaya said
there were different types

66
00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:34.380
of Dials up here.

67
00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:38.430
I wonder if this guy has one
or two stuck to his shoes.

68
00:07:38.510 --> 00:07:40.760
'Cause when he moves,
gusts of wind shoot

69
00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.180
from his feet.

70
00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:45.310
What else could it be?

71
00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:47.600
And those pistols of his
flash as bright as the sun,

72
00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:50.440
blinding me every time he fires.

73
00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:52.120
Where is he now?

74
00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.370
Tiger...

75
00:07:58.450 --> 00:07:59.910
He's using all three?

76
00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.340
...Trap!

77
00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.710
Aren't you a hot shot?

78
00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:24.480
Hah. This Blue Sea idiot
has no clue about using Dials.

79
00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.570
He doesn't even stand a chance.

80
00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.530
Hey! Guess what this is!

81
00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.060
Oh, no!

82
00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.220
It's called a Milky Dial!

83
00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:42.810
You know, aerial combat
isn't just leaping around

84
00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:44.560
out of desperation.

85
00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.480
That looks big.

86
00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:01.450
A ton of wood,
and these things would make

87
00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:03.340
for a killer barbeque.

88
00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:28.640
That was stupid.
Wh-What's wrong with me?

89
00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:30.730
This guy's
already faster than me,

90
00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:33.940
and I hang myself
out like an easy target.

91
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.330
Ugh. And I got
a bullet in my leg.

92
00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:38.000
Agh. Genius.

93
00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:41.590
Gotta be something I can do
about those flashing pistols.

94
00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:43.530
Hold on.

95
00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:46.620
Those guns of yours
are pretty nice accessories.

96
00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:51.320
But too bad for you.

97
00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:53.790
I found my lucky goggles.

98
00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.900
Which means
your little blinding trick...

99
00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:58.910
...won't work on me anymore.

100
00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:01.140
You might as well give up.

101
00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.040
Those just
look like regular goggles.

102
00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:06.000
He found me out!

103
00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:09.580
Not a big fan of
my flash guns are you?

104
00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:12.150
Being a swordsman, you
need close quarters to fight,

105
00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:14.030
which I won't give you.

106
00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:16.110
I don't understand your
reasons for being here

107
00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:17.490
and I don't care.

108
00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:19.530
But I will say that your mere
presence defines you as

109
00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:22.160
an enemy of the Shandorians.

110
00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:24.870
Now I'm telling you,
surrender or die.

111
00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:27.540
Which might happen sooner
if we keep standing here.

112
00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:30.750
That leg of yours
isn't getting any better.

113
00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:34.670
Doesn't hurt too bad.
Barely made a dent.

114
00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:36.630
Getting shot while
I made smug comments about

115
00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:40.300
some big dead eel proves
I'm lacking in concentration.

116
00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:44.050
All right.
Guess I found the perfect

117
00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:47.720
situation to test
that technique again.

118
00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:49.660
Let's give it a try.

119
00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:11.360
Hmph!

120
00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.070
Think you can run away?

121
00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:15.970
Sight.

122
00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:17.890
Sound. Smell.

123
00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:20.570
Taste. Touch. And thought.

124
00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:24.660
These six roots ground us all by
way of good, evil, and peace.

125
00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:26.120
What are you talking about?

126
00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:30.130
And of course, each can
either be pure or impure.

127
00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:33.450
These are the
36 earthly desires.

128
00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:36.200
Hmph.

129
00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:38.290
Listen up, I have
the barrel of a cannon

130
00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:40.420
aimed directly at your head.

131
00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:43.340
And all you have
are a couple of pistols.

132
00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:46.560
In both distance and power,
my weapon's superior.

133
00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:48.600
You've done very well.

134
00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:51.470
But you're still gonna die.

135
00:11:51.550 --> 00:11:52.590
Hmph.

136
00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.280
What cannon?

137
00:11:58.560 --> 00:11:59.850
You're outta your mind.

138
00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:03.330
All I see are three swords.

139
00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:07.250
Have you ever seen
a Flying Blade Attack?

140
00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:08.540
Attack this!

141
00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.750
Single sword style.

142
00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:22.680
Thirty-six caliber phoenix!

143
00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:42.290
That looked uncomfortable.

144
00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:45.340
Nothing personal,
being natural enemies and, all.

145
00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:48.250
But you're in the dirt 'cause
I hate being told what to do.

146
00:12:48.340 --> 00:12:49.800
No other reason.

147
00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:56.390
I'll survive. You watch.

148
00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:17.990
[distant gunfire, explosions

149
00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:19.290
Hmph!

150
00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:25.810
Where am I?

151
00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:27.000
Hm?

152
00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:28.240
I've lost
all sense of direction.

153
00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:31.070
The trees are too tall
for me to see the sun.

154
00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:32.530
Help!

155
00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:35.410
Luffy! Zoro! Robin!
Please find me!

156
00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.830
I don't wanna be left on this
stinking island just to die

157
00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:40.080
and turn into food
for gigantic bugs.

158
00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:43.170
And if I do die, will there even
be a doctor waiting for me?

159
00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:44.710
Wait, it doesn't matter.

160
00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:46.670
When you're dead, you're dead,
and no doctor can save you.

161
00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:48.250
But I don't wanna die!

162
00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:50.370
Now I'm stuck in this awful
place, thinking about death

163
00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:53.220
and doctors, and wondering: Why
couldn't I be something else?

164
00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.140
Like a dentist.
Dentist would be nice.

165
00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:57.200
Poke peoples teeth.
Make them feel better.

166
00:13:57.280 --> 00:14:00.740
No giant sky sharks and
winged people trying to kill me.

167
00:14:00.930 --> 00:14:02.510
At least I got my stick.

168
00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:05.850
Wait. Maybe I've already died
and gone to Heaven.

169
00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:08.020
These look like ruins.

170
00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:09.850
We were supposed
to meet at ruins!

171
00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:12.630
Maybe they're
already here waiting for me!

172
00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:14.820
Or maybe I was
so fast I beat them!

173
00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:17.400
I'm so impressed with
my shrewd navigational skills,

174
00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:18.990
they led me to just
the right place.

175
00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:20.200
This is awesome!

176
00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:23.200
I'm right!
I'm the first one here!

177
00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:27.620
A raccoon-dog?

178
00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:32.420
Gum Gum...

179
00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:35.170
...Balloon!

180
00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:41.790
I can do this
all day if you want,

181
00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:43.130
but you can't win.

182
00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:45.920
Rifles and cannons won't
leave a scratch on me.

183
00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:47.090
Rubber body and all.

184
00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:49.130
So it would seem.

185
00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:51.590
Time for a change of tactics.

186
00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:54.930
Hmm?

187
00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:03.830
Gross! What is that smell?

188
00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:05.870
This weapon
is called the burn bazooka.

189
00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:08.330
By igniting the gas released
from the breath dial,

190
00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:10.380
a deadly blue flame is created.

191
00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:13.630
Which will incinerate anything
in it's path instantly.

192
00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:17.090
Let's see if you can
bounce this back at me.

193
00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:34.730
What the heck is that thing?

194
00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:37.390
It burned right
through that giant tree.

195
00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:41.450
Where'd he go?

196
00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:51.140
Gum-gum...

197
00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.810
...Pistol!

198
00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:02.110
Gum-gum...

199
00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:03.880
Gum-gum...

200
00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:05.470
...Stamp!

201
00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:28.550
That was close.

202
00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.760
Gum-gum...

203
00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:33.720
...Spear!

204
00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:53.520
So you like bazookas, huh?

205
00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:55.690
Get a load of this!

206
00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:57.350
Now, you die!

207
00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:59.750
Gum-gum...

208
00:16:59.940 --> 00:17:02.860
Burn...

209
00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:08.910
– ...Bazooka!
– ...Bazooka!

210
00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:28.990
Straw Hat!

211
00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:36.240
That bastard's dead.

212
00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.460
Sanji!

213
00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:50.670
Sanji!

214
00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:56.280
Sanji?!

215
00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:58.530
No, Sanji! Get up, please!

216
00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:04.830
This is bad! This is really bad!

217
00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:06.330
Sanji!

218
00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:15.200
I... I can't even
hear his heart beating.

219
00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:16.530
It can't be!

220
00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:25.270
What a foolishly angry man.

221
00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:27.150
If I'd come here today
and brought with me pain

222
00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:31.490
and destruction, it would have
been the first thing you felt.

223
00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:34.660
Then why are you here, Eneru?

224
00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:40.070
I expected a warmer hello.

225
00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:46.460
It has been six years
now, my former God...

226
00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:47.920
...Gan Fall.
